 "root_cause": "Worker ok=false replies did not validate their error identity. Missing and non-string error codes were defaulted or stringified into business failures, leaving malformed-protocol workers reusable and classifying real jobs failed rather than unknown.",
 "changes": [
  "Require failed worker replies to carry an explicit 1..80-character lowercase ASCII identifier code",
  "Reject missing/null/non-string/empty/invalid/overlong error identities as malformed protocol",
  "Use the existing protocol-failure reclamation path and retain unknown/media_processing_failed without inventing a business error code",
  "Preserve precise valid business codes, live-worker reuse, budgets and no automatic replay"
 ],
